# RecycleConnect — Frontend

Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS build for the RecycleConnect Admin Dashboard.

## ⚠️ Before you touch anything

1. Install the **Live Server** extension in VS Code (by Ritwick Dey).
2. Always open pages with **"Open with Live Server"** (right-click the file → Open with Live Server). **Never double-click to open a file directly** — the shared sidebar/topbar won't load if you do, since they rely on `fetch()`, which browsers block on `file://` paths.

## Folder structure

```
/
  dashboard.html
  /pages
    /collection-partners
      collection-partners.html
      collection-partners.css
      collection-partners.js
    /recycler-organisations
    /households
    /transactions
    /disputes
    /settings
  /components          ← DO NOT EDIT unless you're Frontend Lead
    sidebar.html
    topbar.html
    style.css
    include.js
  /assets
    /logo
```

## Working on your own page

1. Your page file, CSS, and JS already exist inside `/pages/your-page-name/`.
2. **Only edit inside your own folder.** Never touch anything in `/components/`.
3. Paste this exact boilerplate into your page's `<head>` and `<body>` (adjust the title, CSS/JS filenames, and `data-page-title` to match your page):

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Your Page Name</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&family=Roboto:ital,wght@0,100..900;1,100..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../components/style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="your-page-name.css">
</head>
<body data-page-title="Your Page Name">
    <div id="sidebar-placeholder"></div>

    <div class="main-content">
        <div id="topbar-placeholder"></div>

        <main class="page-content">
            <!-- start your work here -->
        </main>
    </div>

    <script src="../../components/include.js"></script>
    <script src="your-page-name.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

4. Add your own CSS rules inside your page's own `.css` file — never inside `components/style.css`.
5. If you need JS specific to your page, write it in your page's own `.js` file — it loads *after* `include.js`, so the sidebar/topbar will already be in the DOM by the time your script runs (though not guaranteed instantly, since `fetch()` is asynchronous — if you need to reliably wait for them, ask Frontend Lead).

## Git workflow

1. Clone the repo, then create your own branch before making changes:
   ```
   git checkout -b feature/your-page-name
   ```
2. Commit and push your branch:
   ```
   git add .
   git commit -m "Build out collection partners page"
   git push origin feature/your-page-name
   ```
3. Open a Pull Request into `main` on GitHub. Frontend Lead will review and merge.
4. **Never push directly to `main`.**

## Rules recap

- ✅ Edit only your own `/pages/your-folder/` files
- ✅ Open pages with Live Server, not by double-clicking
- ❌ Don't edit `sidebar.html`, `topbar.html`, `style.css` (shared), or `include.js`
- ❌ Don't push directly to `main`